   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601WdT",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "My job, as the MP for Auckland Central and Green Co-Leader, is bringing people together to solve problems and achieve our potential. This election, New Zealanders can agree on basic non-negotiables that we're willing to fight for not only for ourselves, but for all of us. That is how we will reset the rules for the wellbeing of people and planet, breaking the economic doom loop producing the cost of living and climate crises."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601WiX",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I have a proven track record of working hard, bridging the political and bureaucratic divide and getting things done. In Auckland Central, I've worked with residents, businesses and local government to restore the St James Theatre and support our small businesses through COVID, construction and economic challenges... In Parliament, I successfully led work on drug harm reduction, established the pastoral care code for student accommodation, drafted the Bill to end greyhound racing and much more."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601Wnb",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Everyone should be housed, have access to education and work and support, to achieve their potential."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601Wsf",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Vibrancy, supporting both safety and the local economy, especially through filling commercial spaces."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601Wxj",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Healthy nature: a restored Hauraki Gulf, flourishing green space, and real climate resilience."
     }
    ],
