   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601X7r",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "Now is a time where incredible modern challenges have arrived at our doorstep. I believe I can contribute to, or be part of the solution to tackling some of these challenges. I believe in inclusive representation, effective decision-making, and politicians who actually want to be servants of the people. Instead of focusing on what \"isn't possible\", I want to look towards what we can do, and focus on moving our country forward."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601XCv",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I started out my professional career as a journalist, so I have significant experience asking challenging questions and investigating difficult topics. I've also learnt how to listen when it really matters, and I know how to manage and deal with people from all walks of life. Importantly, I'm not a career politician. I'm a normal New Zealander who's lived all his life in Auckland, who wants to do some good for his fellow Kiwis."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601XHz",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Advocate for good urban design to deliver a climate-resilient city, focused on a solar punk future."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601XN3",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Create more safe spaces for all, and provide greater access to the fundamentals for human dignity."
     },
     {
      "_key": "lXvsWGt582gEfwb3601XS7",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Drive democratic engagement, civic education, and social cohesion to tackle big challenges, together."
     }
    ],
